{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CmVeoxGbPpAfdpSWNmyrpi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me construct the worst-tier predictions for each planned experiment. The key constraints from the worst tier definition are:\n\n1. Large model probe AUROC noisy, limited improvement over 7B\n2. Pareto frontier noisy on both architectures (rho near zero or inconsistent)\n3. CaCLR fails AND linear projection unstable on low/mid-resource\n4. CKA partial correlation n.s. after controlling depth\n5. Control task reveals >30% capacity artifacts, low-resource almost all affected\n6. Decomposition dominated by noise\n\n\n7. Orthogonality cosine > 0.15 in some languages (not universal)\n\nNow I'm mapping these constraints against the metric ranges I have for the experiments—the English probe AUROC should stay in the noisier band around 0.72-0.78, zero-shot transfer performance will be weak at 0.56-0.63 across languages, and the Pareto frontier correlations will be scattered with weak or negative Spearman rho values depending on architecture. Now I'm mapping out the full set of planned experiments across different model architectures and analysis approaches—covering Pareto frontier explorations for Qwen and Llama, specialized analyses for calibration, difficulty decomposition, orthogonality properties, and extending the control task validation across multiple languages and larger models. Let me generate the complete YAML configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9539,"cache_read_input_tokens":31590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9539},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1e44a8f-6c4b-4ca5-9efa-f7